 treatment and control systems, solutions, and services, as well as intelligent control solutions. It also provides engineered and configured products and solutions, including dampers and diverters, expansion joints, selective catalytic reduction systems, severe-service and industrial cyclones, dust collectors, thermal oxidizers, filtration systems, wet and dry scrubbers, separators and coalescers, water treatment packages, metallic and non-metallic pumps, industrial silencers, and fluid handling equipment, as well as plant engineering services and engineered design build fabrication services. In addition, the company offers solutions for air pollution and contamination control, fluid handling, and process filtration in various applications, such as aluminum beverage can production, automobile production, food and beverage processing, semiconductor fabrication, electronics production, steel and aluminum mill processing, wood manufacturing, desalination, and aquaculture markets, as well as it provides engineered industrial process heating solutions for process industries. It markets its power generation, hydrocarbon processing, water/wastewater treatment, oily water separation and treatment, marine and naval vessels, and midstream oil and gas sectors. CECO Environmental Corp. was founded in 1869 and is headquartered in Addison, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Todd R. Gleason | CEO & Chairman | Age 54 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $503K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 13%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["CECO Environmental Corp. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $2.6B market cap on $774M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 32%.","The company is burning through $5M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 148% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.4753403933434188},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $7.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-7678718.26},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.